.turbo
.git
# Both the bare and `**/` forms are needed: .dockerignore patterns are matched
# against the path relative to the context root, so `.env` alone matches only
# a root-level file and would let apps/api/.env — which holds real local
# secrets — into the build context. The multi-stage builds happen not to copy
# it into any final image, but nothing enforces that.
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*
!.env.example
!**/.env.example
*.log
.DS_Store
apps/api/uploads

# The client's original reference images. Gitignored, but .dockerignore is a
# separate list — Docker never reads .gitignore — so without this line they
# are copied into `public/` and served publicly by the web image. That
# includes the model shot the client explicitly withheld (ADR-0026), which
# would be reachable at /reference/... on the live site. Everything derived
# from these ships as the cropped WEBPs under public/images/ instead.
apps/web/public/reference
